NAME
    lang-set - query or change the selected global language

SYNOPSIS
    lang-set
    lang-set <locale>

DESCRIPTION
    With no operands, lang-set writes the locale selected by the sys language
    selector and a newline.

    With one locale operand, lang-set validates every materialized global
    res/<owner>/lang tree before changing any selector. The requested locale
    must exist in every participating tree and every existing current selector
    must be a valid local relative symbolic link.

    Non-sys selectors are updated first and the sys selector is updated last.
    Preparation errors leave every selector unchanged. On an ordinary update
    error the command attempts rollback and reports rollback failure separately.
    Successful selection writes no output.

    Package-local language resources are not modified.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m lang-set [arguments].


EXIT STATUS

    Bootstrap failures (before operation dispatch):
    1    m_ROOT is missing or empty; invoke the command through m or
         from an initialized m environment.
    2    The m shell runtime could not be loaded.
    Operation-specific failures below may also use these numeric
    statuses; stderr identifies the bootstrap or operation branch.

    0   Query or selection succeeded.
    1   Invalid argument count.
    2   Requested locale is unavailable in a participating owner.
    3   A selector or selector path is structurally invalid.
    4   Selector preparation failed before updates began.
    5   Selector update failed and rollback completed.
    6   Selector update and rollback both failed.
        Distinct language.* diagnostic identities identify each failure class.

SEE ALSO
    lang
